I can’t call the Rhylthyme tools in this session, so there is no live URL or tool-output Gantt/itinerary. The program below is the deliverable to run through `validate_program`, `analyze_schedule`, and `visualize_schedule` when those tools are available.

Improved question: “For every shared resource and every human cue, what actually has to be true at the start of each step, not just what the explicit clock offsets say?” That exposes the hidden dependencies: canapés must finish before the room call; the room call and table dressing must finish before seating; seating must start before starter plating and finish before the toast; starter clearing gates main plating; main clearing gates first dance; the dance floor must clear first dance and cake cutting before dancing; the microphone must be free for toast and speeches; and dessert plating must be gated to the cake-cutting moment rather than occurring early. I therefore use `compound` waits for multi-condition gates, `event:"start"` for “after it starts” and “when it goes out,” and an inferred MC sound check as one obvious ready-at-the-same-moment step. The exact finish cannot be scheduled because the source never states the band’s last-set time, so `dancing` is `indefinite`.

